# Project: EZ Wonders — kids' numeracy game platform

## Repo layout (READ THIS FIRST — it is not what "monorepo" implies)

The workspace root **IS the frontend**. There is no `games/` subfolder.

- workspace root (`d:/Phaser/games`) — Vite + React frontend, deployed to Netlify-style static hosting at `ezwonders.com`
- `../../K1 games project/server/` — Node/Express + Mongoose backend, deployed on Render

Because the server is *outside* the workspace, tools cannot read it by default and
edits to it are not part of this repo. Do not assume a server change is testable
from here. When reasoning about the API, read the actual server file rather than
trusting any doc (including this one) — it has drifted repeatedly.

Stale/ignored artifacts to leave alone unless asked: `dist/`, `_sout.log`,
`server/IMPLEMENTATION_PROMPT.md`, `server/SETUP.md`, `server/logPlaySession.js`
(a stale, much older copy of the frontend file — it still exports, but nothing
imports it, so edits there change nothing).

Do not re-explain React/Tailwind/Express basics below. Only project-specific
architecture. If unsure whether a helper exists, read the file before writing a
new one — several near-duplicates were consolidated recently and re-adding one
would undo that.

## Stack (frontend)

react 19, react-router-dom v7, zustand v5 (+persist), tailwindcss v4 via
`@tailwindcss/vite` (NOT the v3 postcss workflow — no `tailwind.config.js`;
theme lives in CSS via `@import "tailwindcss"` and `@theme`), motion
(`import { motion } from 'motion/react'`), phaser v4, @dnd-kit/* (admin panel
drag-reorder), react-confetti, use-sound, react-helmet-async, clsx +
tailwind-merge, react-qr-code, jspdf + html-to-image (student badge export only),
react-use.

## Stack (server)

Express + Mongoose. **Auth is not JWT/session-based.** Every write endpoint
re-validates a code against the DB per request, via `requireTeacher` /
`requireAdmin` middleware in `server.js`.

## Core domain model (post class-scoping migration)

**`classType` is DEPRECATED.** It still exists on `ClassInfo` (`enum: ['k1','k2']`)
and on `GameAccess` purely so legacy documents validate and a bad migration can be
rolled back. It no longer drives game access or permissions. All live logic keys
on `classId`. Never write new code that keys off classType.

- **`ClassInfo`**: `classId` (unique), `className`, `classAlias` (short label),
  `classYear`, `classCode` (globally unique login code, sparse), `isPublic`
  (public = join with name + classCode; private = needs an individual student
  code), `active` (soft-retire, never delete), `image` (null until uploaded —
  render a placeholder), `classType` (deprecated). The teacher list is **derived**
  by querying `Teacher` for a matching `classId`, never stored on the class.
- **`Teacher`**: `code` (unique), `name`, `classId` (**null for the global
  admin**), `role: 'teacher' | 'admin'`, `active` (soft-deactivate so historical
  stats rows still resolve). Only one admin code exists; it comes from the
  `ADMIN_CODE` env var via a boot migration. There is no seeded teacher list.
- **`Student`**: `studentId` (server-generated UUID, not Mongo `_id`), `classId`,
  `fullName`, `nickname`, `group` (freeform label, no behaviour), `code`
  (6-char, unique, sparse — drives `/p/:code` student auto-login), plus
  `mergedInto` / `mergedAt` / `mergedBy` merge bookkeeping. Merged-away records
  are **never deleted**, so a merge stays reversible.
- **`GameAccess`**: **classId-scoped** — one row per `{classId, gameKey}` under a
  *partial* unique index (`partialFilterExpression: { classId: { $exists: true } }`).
  The partial filter is load-bearing: legacy rows that carry only `classType` and
  no `classId` are retained for rollback and must not collide. `added` (opted in
  from the catalogue — a class only sees games it has added), `unlocked`,
  `shiny` (featured), `order`, `unlockAt`.
- **`PlaySession`**: one row per completed round, `classId`-scoped (`game`,
  `playerName`, `studentId`, `classId`, `stars`, `totalRounds`, `peakStreak`,
  optional `elapsedSeconds`/`mistakes`, `device`).
- **`PlayerMerge`**: merge/link records so a "light" name-only identity can be
  bound to a rostered `studentId` after the fact.
- **`SystemConfig`**: maintenance mode, polled live.
- **Legacy default**: `classId: 'k12026-pny'` is the fallback when a classId is
  missing client-side (see `LEGACY_CLASS_ID` in `logPlaySession.js`).

## Scheduled unlocks

`GameAccess.unlockAt` (Date, nullable) is the only field this feature added. A row
with `unlockAt` set is **always** `unlocked: false` — the schedule is a promise to
flip it later, not a parallel state.

- Unlocking early clears `unlockAt`; removing a game or re-adding it also clears it.
- Due unlocks are applied **lazily on read** by `resolveDueUnlocks()` inside
  `getGameAccessRows()`. **There is no cron**, so a schedule still fires correctly
  after the server slept through the exact minute.
- Because of that, every read path returning game rows must auto-unlock first.
  Do not add a read path that queries `GameAccess` directly and skips it.
- `PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey/schedule` rejects a past time (400) and an
  already-unlocked game (409). It must stay **above** `/api/game-access/:gameKey`
  in `server.js` (Express matches in registration order).
- The same endpoint **cancels** a schedule when sent `unlockAt: null`, clearing
  the field without unlocking the game (404 if nothing was scheduled). A cancel
  is deliberately NOT sent as a past time — past times are rejected, and
  "unlock it now" is a different, destructive intent.
- `GameAccess` reads are guarded by a per-process `pendingUnlockCache`. **Any new
  write path that can change `unlockAt` MUST call `invalidateUnlockCache(classId)`.**

## Auth model

**Identity kinds** — `POST /api/code-lookup` classifies a code into exactly one:
`teacherCode`, `adminCode`, `studentCode`, or `classCode`. A bare `classCode` is
not a session; it branches the login flow to either a name (public class) or a
student code (private class).

- `isTeacher` / `isAdmin` in the zustand store are **UI state only, not a security
  boundary**. Every write endpoint re-validates the code server-side.
- **Teacher** (`requireTeacher`): view their own class info, manage their own
  roster, and view/edit their own class's game arrangement. Scoped to their own
  `classId`.
- **Admin** (`requireAdmin`, stricter — `role` must be `'admin'`): manages any
  class, regardless of whether it is their homeroom. The admin's `classId` is
  **null**, which is why any component that resolves a class-scoped thing must
  handle the no-class case (e.g. `NextGameTimer` self-hides for them, and
  `GameAccessGate` lets teachers/admins through *before* its loading gate — an
  admin has no classId, so game-access never loads for them and they would
  otherwise spin forever).
- Login: `NameGate.jsx` posts to `/api/code-lookup` (and `/api/student-login` for
  the light path). The server returns the full identity. **There is no client-side
  hardcoded teacher-code mirror** — the file that did this (`src/teacherCodes.js`)
  was deleted, because the frontend copy drifted from the DB and locked out
  newly-added teachers. Do not reintroduce one.

## Frontend gating flow

`NameGate.jsx` (whole-app entry, also wraps every game) captures a code, or a
name + public class code, and persists **only the credential** in `playerStore.js`.
`GameAccessGate.jsx` wraps each game and re-checks per-game unlock via
`useIsGameUnlocked`. Both gates independently re-fetch if data isn't loaded for
the current classId. New game routes need **both gates, in that order**:
`NameGate` → `GameAccessGate` → game.

`playerStore.js` persists only `{code, name, mode}` — the credential needed to
re-resolve the identity from the DB on every load. Names, classIds and roles are
**runtime-only** so that removing a student or changing a code signs that device
out on its next validation. The persist `name`/`version` are bumped **only** to
force a global re-login (that is what `version: 3` was); changing either logs
every device out.

## Key frontend files

- `src/apiClient.js` — **the single source of truth for `API_BASE`, `withQuery`,
  `fetchWithTimeout`, `requestJson`, `postJson` and `ApiError`.** Always import
  from here. Never redeclare an API origin or roll a new timeout: this is exactly
  what drifted before (12s / 15s / *no timeout at all*), and the missing one hung
  app boot, since `AuthBootstrap` blocks the entire render on `hydrate()`.
- `src/playerStore.js` — persisted credential + runtime identity.
- `src/gameAccess.js` — `GAME_CATALOG` (canonical game list: key, emoji, label,
  subtitle, hue, gradient, `to`, `progressKey`), the classId-based read store used
  by Home/`GameAccessGate`, plus class-scoped mutators used only by the panel.
  Also `nextScheduledGame(games)` / `useNextScheduledGame()`,
  `useGameByKey()`, and `formatUnlockCountdown()`.
- `src/logPlaySession.js` — called by every game on completion
  (`logPlaySession({game, ...})`), plus `fetchStats` / `fetchSummary` /
  `fetchPlaysPage` / `fetchLeaderboard` / `fetchAdminClassStats`.
- `src/students.js`, `src/classInfo.js` — roster + class/system API stores.
- `src/systemConfig.js` — maintenance mode, cached to localStorage then corrected.
- `src/main.jsx` — all routes lazy-loaded, `AuthBootstrap`, and **two**
  `ErrorBoundary`s (app-level + per-route) so a failed lazy chunk can't blank the
  app. Wrap new top-level surfaces in one.
- `src/BetaHome.jsx` — the real home at `/`. Large; holds the SVG `Icon` library,
  card gradients, the aurora backdrop layers, and `SwitchPlayerButton` (the
  shared-device "not you?" affordance — it already exists, don't add another).
- `src/GameAccessPanel.jsx` — admin panel: tab bar is **"K1 Games" / "K2 Games" /
  Students / Settings** (separate top-level tabs, each independently editable,
  defaulting to the admin's own class). Non-admin teachers see a single read-only
  **"Games"** tab for their own class — no drag/lock/shiny controls, just static
  badges.
- `src/TeacherOnboarding.jsx` (`/teacher-onboarding`) — the public teacher guide.
  **Copy and imagery live in `teacherOnboardingContent.js`**
  (`ONBOARDING_SECTIONS` + `ONBOARDING_GIFS`), not in the component. An empty GIF
  string renders the "coming soon" placeholder automatically; a broken URL falls
  back via `onError`. The page is deliberately public and is listed in
  `PUBLIC_DURING_MAINTENANCE` in `MaintenanceGate.jsx`.
  **Never rename the content file to `teacherOnboarding.js`** — it would differ
  from the component only by case, and on a case-insensitive filesystem an
  extension-less `./TeacherOnboarding` import can resolve to it.
- `src/Phaser/common/` — shared Phaser helpers: `audioState.js` (mute + bg music),
  `numbersVoice.js`, `speech.js`, `sceneAssets.js`, `starProgress.js`,
  `uiHelpers.js`.
- Phaser games live under `BonusGames/<name>/GamePage.jsx` (including Game4, which
  is not labelled "bonus"). `GamePage.jsx` wraps the canvas in page chrome and
  composes `NameGate` → `GameAccessGate` → `Game`. The page paints no background,
  so the platform backdrop shows through; each game paints its own art inside the
  canvas.

## Server endpoint contract

Admin-only unless noted. All return `{ error: '...' }` with non-2xx on failure.

Auth / codes
- `POST /api/code-lookup` — **rate-limited.** Classifies a code into one identity kind.
- `POST /api/teacher-login` — **rate-limited.** `{code}` → identity or 401.
- `POST /api/student-login` — **rate-limited.** Public-class light login.
- `GET /api/student-login/:code` — student auto-login via `/p/:code`.
- `POST /api/codes/check` — "is this code free?" across the whole namespace.

Classes
- `GET /api/classes`, `GET /api/classes/:classId`, `POST /api/classes`,
  `PUT /api/classes/:classId`, `PATCH /api/classes/:classId/public`,
  `PATCH /api/classes/:classId/code`.

Students / identities (teacher-scoped to their own class)
- `GET|POST /api/students`, `PUT|DELETE /api/students/:studentId`
- `GET /api/classes/:classId/identities` — roster + name-only identities
- `GET|POST /api/classes/:classId/students`, `PUT|DELETE .../students/:studentId`
- `POST /api/classes/:classId/students/merge`, `POST .../unmerge`
- `DELETE /api/classes/:classId/identities/:name` — deletes a **name-only
  ("light") identity** by removing its play sessions, since that history is the
  only thing that makes it exist. 409s if the name still matches a roster student
  (delete the student instead). Matches `classId` against both the URL param and
  the actor's own classId — the two aren't always the same string, which is why
  this one endpoint is defensive.

Game access
- `GET /api/game-access?classId=` — read; returns that class's rows (auto-unlocks first).
- `PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey` — set `unlocked`
- `PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey/shiny`
- `PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey/schedule` — sets `unlockAt`. Rejects past (400) /
  already-unlocked (409). **Must stay above `/api/game-access/:gameKey`.**
- `PUT /api/game-access/order` — **must stay above `/api/game-access/:gameKey`.**
- `POST|DELETE /api/game-access/:gameKey` — add from catalogue / remove

Plays / stats
- `POST /api/plays` — **rate-limited.** Logs a session; falls back to the legacy
  class if `classId` is absent client-side.
- `DELETE /api/plays` — delete one player's records for one game.
- `GET /api/stats` — teacher admin-style totals + per-game breakdown
- `GET /api/summary` — teacher code → paginated `{rows,total,page,limit,hasMore}`;
  `classId` + `playerName` → plain unpaginated array
- `GET /api/plays` — paginated individual sessions
- `GET /api/leaderboard`, `/api/leaderboard/:game`, `/api/player/weekly`,
  `/api/weekly-mission`
- `GET /api/admin/stats/classes`, `/api/admin/stats/classes/:classId`

System
- `GET|PATCH /api/system/config` (maintenance mode), `POST /api/feedback`
  (**rate-limited**), `GET /api/ping`, `/api/health`.

**Rate limits apply only to the unauthenticated/abuse-prone routes:** `code-lookup`,
`teacher-login`, `student-login`, `plays`, `feedback`. Do **not** add limits to
authenticated write paths — a whole class can legitimately burst through
`/api/plays`, and a per-IP cap would throttle everyone behind one school NAT.

## Mongoose / Mongo gotchas

- Nested subdocument fields must avoid a key literally named `type` (Mongoose reads
  it as a type-declaration shorthand) — see `PlaySession.device.kind`, not `.type`.
- **Schema field changes do not migrate indexes.** A Mongoose schema edit alone
  will not drop or rebuild an existing index in MongoDB; that must be done
  explicitly, then `syncIndexes()` called.
- One-time data migrations run at boot in the `mongoose.connect().then()` chain,
  **before `app.listen`**, and must be self-guarding/idempotent — check for the
  absence of the new field or presence of the old one before acting, so redeploys
  don't redo or corrupt the migration.
- When you add an enum value (e.g. a role) remember the boot replay path that
  applies enum changes to existing documents.

## Conventions

- Comments explain **why**, not what — short rationale above non-obvious logic.
- Prefer extending the existing zustand store / API helper file over creating a
  parallel one. One store per domain, one thin fetch-helper file per API concern,
  and **one** shared `apiClient.js`.
- Env: `VITE_API_BASE_URL` (frontend, defaults to `http://localhost:4000`),
  `MONGODB_URI`, `ADMIN_CODE` and `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (backend).
- **`frontend .env` IS COMMITTED and must stay committed.** It holds only the
  public API origin, and it is the only place a deployed build can read it from
  — this project sets no host-side frontend env. Untracking it makes production
  fall back to `http://localhost:4000`, which every request fails against and
  the browser reports as a **CORS error**, pointing at the server instead of at
  the missing config. Private values go in `.env.local` (gitignored) or the
  backend host's own env (`ALLOWED_ORIGINS` etc.).
- **`cn()` lives in `src/cn.js`.** Import it; never redefine it. `clsx` and
  `tailwind-merge` should be imported by that one file only.
- **Fonts: Fredoka only, loaded once in `index.html`.** Never add a `<link>` to
  Google Fonts from a component — it can't start until that lazy chunk has
  executed, so the font competes with the page and text re-flows on arrival. The
  `.font-heading` / `.font-body` utilities are declared in `src/index.css` and are
  both Fredoka; do **not** re-declare them in a component's inline `<style>` (that
  duplicate was removed from ~15 files). Nunito is not loaded and must not be
  referenced.
- **`localStorage` keys** are namespaced and shared where the concept is shared.
  The mute preference uses one key (`ezw-muted-v1` in
  `Phaser/common/audioState.js`) because mute is a property of the player, not of
  whichever game they are in. Never give a game its own mute key.

## Performance / platform notes

- `vite.config.js` sets `manualChunks` as a **function** — Vite 8 bundles with
  rolldown, which rejects the Rollup object form with "manualChunks is not a function".
- `vite-plugin-pwa` ships the service worker. Phaser (~1.4MB) is excluded from
  precaching via `globIgnores` and cached at runtime on first real play, because
  eager precaching would push that onto every visitor including those who never
  open a game. The API is never cached (`navigateFallbackDenylist`).
- `public/site.webmanifest` is hand-maintained and linked from `index.html`;
  `VitePWA` is configured with `manifest: false` so it does not generate a second one.
- **Canonical/robots are per-route** via `src/seo.jsx`; add a public route to
  `INDEXABLE_ROUTES` there **and** to `public/sitemap.xml`, or it will be marked
  `noindex` and pointed at the root canonical.
- DevOptions for the service worker are disabled in dev so a stale module graph
  can't be served while developing.

## The "next game" banner

`NextGameTimer.jsx` is **schedule-driven, not calendar-driven**. The old hardcoded
"new game every Friday" cadence is gone — there is no default cadence.

- It renders **nothing** when the class has no pending schedule; callers gate it on
  `useNextScheduledGame()` so the surrounding layout collapses cleanly. The Weekly
  Champions leaderboard always shows regardless.
- It names the soonest `!unlocked && unlockAt` game and counts down in
  days/hours/mins/secs, then calls `fetchGameAccess()` at zero so the server applies
  the unlock and the banner either rolls on or disappears.
- Teachers see it too (it's a schedule preview); the admin has no class, so it
  self-hides for them.
- Panel control: the clock button in each locked game row opens
  `ScheduleUnlockDialog`. Scheduled rows show an "⏰ Unlocks ..." badge. The button
  is hidden entirely once a game is unlocked. Once a schedule exists, a separate
  cancel button (in the row and in the dialog) clears it while leaving the game
  locked.
- `GameAccessGate` uses `formatUnlockCountdown()` to show a coarse "Ready in 2d 4h"
  on a scheduled game instead of the generic "isn't out yet / ask your teacher".

## Adding a new game — checklist

1. Build the game (React or Phaser) under `src`. Phaser games go in
   `src/BonusGames/<name>/` as `GamePage.jsx` + scenes, even when not labelled "bonus".
2. Add a `lazy()` import + `<Route>` in `main.jsx`.
3. Add an entry to `GAME_CATALOG` in `gameAccess.js` (unique `key`).
4. Compose `NameGate` → `GameAccessGate` (correct `gameNumber`/`gameLabel`).
5. Call `logPlaySession({ game: '<slug>' })` on completion with the matching slug.
6. Use `addMuteButton` / `ensureBgMusic` from `Phaser/common/audioState.js` for
   audio, never a per-game copy.
7. It appears once an **admin** adds it to a class from the Catalogue.
8. Double-check the `title`, on-screen heading and catalogue `label` all agree, and
   that no other game already uses that name — a duplicate name is invisible in the
   panel and has caused a shipped mismatch before.

## Testing

Vitest for pure logic (`npm test`). There is no DOM/E2E suite. Prefer testing pure
functions — `mergeRows`, `nextScheduledGame`, `formatUnlockCountdown`, the round
generators in the `levels.js` files, and the device fingerprint. `vite build` and
`npm run lint` run in CI; both must pass.

## Pushing code

Only push when the user explicitly says so. Trigger phrases: "push the code",
"push it", "push both ends", "push everything", or any "push" command.

Run the three commands **as three separate `execute_command` calls, never chained**
(chaining with `;` breaks `git commit -m`). In each repo, in order:

1. `git add .`
2. `git commit -m "<concise summary of changes>"`
3. `git push origin main`

Repo = current working context: frontend `d:/Phaser/games` and/or backend
`D:\K1 games project\server`. "both ends" / "both" / "everything" = do the
frontend first, then the backend. Skip `commit`/`push` if a repo's working tree
is clean ("nothing to commit").
